wercase"]},{"def":"The name of the Latin script letter A/a.","dna16":"8800000344000323","ex":[],"id":"wikt:a:noun:3","pos":"noun","src":"wikt","sym":"","syn":[]},{"def":"An unspecified example of (something); the indefinite article.","dna16":"8800000344000422","ex":["There was a man here looking for you yesterday.","Hoots the Owl: Yes a, fruit, is a , any, time, food!"],"id":"wikt:a:article:4","pos":"article","src":"wikt","sym":"38:1","syn":["an","one"]},{"def":"One; used before score, dozen, hundred, thousand, million, etc.","dna16":"8800000344000521","ex":["I've seen it happen a hundred times."],"id":"wikt:a:article:5","pos":"article","src":"wikt","sym":"4:1","syn":["an","one"]},{"def":"Used in some phrases denoting quantity, such as a few, a good many, a couple, a little, a bit, etc.","dna16":"8800000344000620","ex":["He's a bit thick, isn't he?","They asked me a few questions."],"id":"wikt:a:article:6","pos":"article","src":"wikt","sym":"16:1,17:2,85:1","syn":["an","one"]},{"def":"Used before a numeral.","dna16":"8800000344000729","ex":["There are a few hundred orders that need to be fulfilled by tomorrow."],"id":"wikt:a:article:7","pos":"article","src":"wikt","sym":"4:1","syn":["an","one"]},{"def":"Used in some adverbial phrases denoting the degree or extent of an action, such as a little, a bit, a lot, etc.","dna16":"8800000344000828","ex":["The door was opened a little."],"id":"wikt:a:article:8","pos":"article","src":"wikt","sym":"17:1,85:1","syn":["an","one"]},{"def":"The same; one and the same. Used in phrases such as of a kind, birds of a feather, etc.","dna16":"8800000344000927","ex":["We are of a mind on matters of morals.","They're two of a kind."],"id":"wikt:a:article:9","pos":"article","src":"wikt","sym":"60:2","syn":["an","one"]},{"def":"Any; every; used before a noun which has become modified to limit its scope.","dna16":"8800000344001024","ex":["A man who dies intestate leaves his children troubles and difficulties."],"id":"wikt:a:article:10","pos":"article","src":"wikt","sym":"4:1,12:1,23:1","syn":["an","one"]},{"def":"Any; used with a negative to indicate not a single one.","dna16":"8800000344001123","ex":["It was so dark that we couldn't see a thing.","He fell all that way, and hasn't a bump on his head?"],"id":"wikt:a:article:11","pos":"article","src":"wikt","sym":"","syn":["an","one"]},{"def":"Used before an adjective that modifies a noun (singular or plural) delimited by a numeral.","dna16":"8800000344001222","ex":["The lottery jackpot is worth a staggering three hundred million dollars.","The holidays are a mere one week away."],"id":"wikt:a:article:12","pos":"article","src":"wikt","sym":"4:1","syn":["an","one"]},{"def":"One; someone named; used before a person's name, suggesting that the speaker knows little about the person other than the name.","dna16":"8800000344001321","ex":["We've received an interesting letter from a Mrs. Miggins of London."],"id":"wikt:a:article:13","pos":"article","src":"wikt","sym":"4:1,17:1","syn":["an","one"]},{"def":"Used before an adjective modifying a person's name, typically used to emphasize that person's current condition or emotional state.","dna16":"8800000344001420","ex":[],"id":"wikt:a:article:14","pos":"article","src":"wikt","sym":"4:1,50:1,80:1","syn":["an","one"]},{"def":"Someone or something like; similar to; used before a proper noun to create an example out of it.","dna16":"8800000344001529","ex":["The center of the village was becoming a Times Square.","The man is a regular Romeo."],"id":"wikt:a:article:15","pos":"article","src":"wikt","sym":"4:1,38:1,60:2,74:1","syn":["an","one"]},{"def":"To do with separation; In, into.","dna16":"8800000344001628","ex":["torn a pieces"],"id":"wikt:a:preposition:16","pos":"preposition","src":"wikt","sym":"","syn":[]},{"def":"To do with time; Each, per, in, on, by. Often occurs between two nouns, where the first noun occurs at the end of a verbal phrase.","dna16":"8800000344001727","ex":["I brush my teeth twice a day."],"id